Cell["\<\
The public return value is a presentation Grid. Its rows show the Hamiltonian \
index, site and Wyckoff-orbit indices, equivalent atom, fractional and \
Cartesian positions, local orbital, actual transported basis state, spin \
structure, and transport operation.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"ac36fe71-79af-4230-b1fc-b5d092170dd1"],

Cell["\<\
The Grid is only the display layer. MagneticTB still keeps the model data \
internally as Association and List records; those private records are not a \
second public return format and should not be indexed through the Grid.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"8f9137f8-ec27-4cfb-b936-b8c40261e840"],

Cell["\<\
orbitalTable never solves a bond shell and never changes the current model.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"53292c3c-cb54-4b58-9347-8ea2f02ea65c"],

Cell["\<\
orbitalTable returns $Failed and issues a message when no compatible current \
model exists or the stored Hamiltonian basis order is inconsistent. It does \
not repair the input or switch to an approximate fallback.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"07ade3a4-7340-4da1-9caf-32af50d20cdc"]
}, Closed]],

